  "reason": "R1 establishes that an MTP can attain near-DFT accuracy in a closely related BCC refractory multicomponent alloy, while R2 and R20 indicate that SRO can produce meaningful energetic or transport effects in similar refractory alloys. R12 and R15 provide more general support for finite-temperature electronic free-energy and Fermi-level DOS contributions, and R3/R10 show broader use of machine learning or efficient computational screening. However, none of the records proposes training a liquid-phase MTP to reproduce the DFT phase-space distribution, using the small MTP–DFT energy-difference variance for free-energy perturbation, or replacing thermodynamic integration in a melting-point workflow. Thus the records point toward accurate ML potentials and relevant free-energy corrections, but the combined MTP-FEP intervention and its rapid-convergence mechanism require a substantial new idea."
